From c27ee1cceae87845de90bbcaa81a08dcb12baae6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:19:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] prplmesh: fix cert-mode infinite Channel Scan Abort loop

In certification mode the 2.4GHz radio (phy00.0) can be continuously
commandeered by the apsta/bSTA on the same PHY (wpa_supplicant on wlan0
cycling authenticate -> "AP doesn't support backhaul BSS" -> deauth ->
rescan). As a result the monitor's NL80211 channel-scan trigger for the
EasyMesh On-Request scan never becomes active (m_scan_active stays false),
and the ChannelScanTask radio scan gets stuck in a non-terminal state
(PENDING_TRIGGER / WAIT_FOR_SCAN_TRIGGERED).

Once stuck, the task's per-FSM-tick timeout branch
(channel_scan_task.cpp[181]) re-issued ABORT_CHANNEL_SCAN every ~200ms
forever: abort_scan_request() only sent the CMDU without driving the FSM
to a terminal state, and the monitor's channel_scan_abort() replied
"No active channel scan to abort" and returned success WITHOUT emitting a
Channel_Scan_Aborted event - so the task never received the
ABORTED_NOTIFICATION that is its only route to SCAN_ABORTED. This looped
8+ minutes with no Channel Scan Report ever produced, so MAP-4.14.1
Phase 3 ("MAUT should respond with a Channel Scan Report") timed out with
"Channel Scan Report message from MAUT not found".

Fixes (three complementary changes):

- channel_scan_task.cpp (work), Fix A: after abort_scan_request() on the
  overall SCAN_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SEC, locally set SCAN_ABORTED status and
  FSM_MOVE_STATE to SCAN_ABORTED so the request is finalized (report sent,
  is_scan_currently_running cleared) even without an ABORTED_NOTIFICATION.

- channel_scan_task.cpp (work), Fix C: add a timeout->SCAN_FAILED fallback
  to the PENDING_TRIGGER case (previously empty), gated on the same overall
  request timeout, so a scan whose trigger is never accepted by the driver
  cannot sit in PENDING_TRIGGER indefinitely.

- mon_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp (channel_scan_abort), Fix B: emit
  Event::Channel_Scan_Aborted on the "no active scan" early-return path so
  the agent task's FSM always receives the ABORTED_NOTIFICATION and can
  reach a terminal state.

Together these break the infinite abort loop and guarantee a Channel Scan
Report is produced (empty/failed-status if the radio was busy) instead of
hanging.

Note: breaking the loop makes the MAUT respond; for MAP-4.14.1 to fully
PASS the 2.4GHz apsta/bSTA role must additionally be idle during the scan
window so the scan can actually succeed and carry results.

Signed-off-by: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
